{
  "title": "n8n — Node & Task Runner Latency",
  "uid": "n8n-node-latency",
  "tags": [
    "n8n",
    "tracing",
    "task-runner"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-3h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Prometheus",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "tracesource",
        "label": "Tempo",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "tempo",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "service",
        "label": "n8n instance",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "query": "label_values(traces_spanmetrics_latency_count{span_name=\"node.execute\"}, service)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {}
      },
      {
        "name": "min_duration",
        "label": "Slower than",
        "type": "custom",
        "query": "200ms,500ms,1s,2s,5s",
        "current": {
          "text": "1s",
          "value": "1s"
        },
        "options": [
          {
            "text": "200ms",
            "value": "200ms",
            "selected": false
          },
          {
            "text": "500ms",
            "value": "500ms",
            "selected": false
          },
          {
            "text": "1s",
            "value": "1s",
            "selected": true
          },
          {
            "text": "2s",
            "value": "2s",
            "selected": false
          },
          {
            "text": "5s",
            "value": "5s",
            "selected": false
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard is for",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "n8n's Prometheus metrics stop at the **workflow** boundary. `n8n_workflow_execution_duration_seconds` will tell you an execution took 8 seconds and nothing about where the 8 seconds went, and there are **no task-runner metrics at all** — no `task-runner-metrics.service.js` exists alongside the other 23 in `dist/metrics/prometheus/`.\n\nEverything below is derived from OpenTelemetry spans instead: n8n emits a `node.execute` span per node (`N8N_OTEL_ENABLED`), Tempo's metrics-generator converts those spans into RED metrics and remote-writes them to Prometheus. That is what makes per-node latency queryable and alertable.\n\n**The catch worth knowing:** a Code node is `n8n-nodes-base.code` whether it runs on the JavaScript runner or the Python one, and n8n puts no language attribute on the span. The only thing separating them is the node *name*, which is why `n8n.node.name` is promoted to a metric dimension in `tempo.yaml`."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Node p95 latency by node type",
      "description": "The attribution Prometheus alone cannot give you. Spikes here name the node type responsible for a slow workflow.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (n8n_node_type, le) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_latency_bucket{service=~\"$service\", span_name=\"node.execute\", n8n_node_type!=\"\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{n8n_node_type}}",
          "exemplar": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Code node latency — JavaScript runner vs Python runner",
      "description": "Mean seconds per Code node execution, split by node name because node type cannot distinguish the two runners. The Python runner is a single GIL-bound process with DEFAULT_MAX_CONCURRENCY = 5; the JS runner allows 10.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (n8n_node_name) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_latency_sum{service=~\"$service\", n8n_node_type=\"n8n-nodes-base.code\"}[$__rate_interval])) / sum by (n8n_node_name) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_latency_count{service=~\"$service\", n8n_node_type=\"n8n-nodes-base.code\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{n8n_node_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Slowest nodes (mean over range)",
      "description": "Grouped by node type AND node name, because node type alone cannot separate a Code node on the JavaScript runner from one on the Python runner. Sorted worst first.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "calls/sec"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "reqps"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "sortBy": [
          {
            "displayName": "mean",
            "desc": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "sum by (n8n_node_type, n8n_node_name) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_latency_sum{service=~\"$service\", span_name=\"node.execute\", n8n_node_type!=\"\"}[$__range])) / sum by (n8n_node_type, n8n_node_name) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_latency_count{service=~\"$service\", span_name=\"node.execute\", n8n_node_type!=\"\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "mean"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "sum by (n8n_node_type, n8n_node_name) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_calls_total{service=~\"$service\", span_name=\"node.execute\", n8n_node_type!=\"\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "calls/sec"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "merge",
          "options": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "n8n_node_type": "node type",
              "n8n_node_name": "node name",
              "Value #A": "mean",
              "Value #B": "calls/sec"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Workflow p95 vs per-node p95",
      "description": "Both are 95th percentiles, not a sum: span metrics are pre-aggregated, so node durations cannot be summed per workflow here. Read it as 'how much of a slow workflow is one slow node' - when the two lines track each other, a single node dominates. To see the actual non-node remainder you need the trace, not this panel: use the trace table below.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 14
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_latency_bucket{service=~\"$service\", span_name=\"workflow.execute\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "workflow.execute p95",
          "exemplar": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_latency_bucket{service=~\"$service\", span_name=\"node.execute\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "node.execute p95 (any single node)",
          "exemplar": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Node executions per second by type",
      "description": "Throughput, for reading the latency panels in context — a p95 spike on two calls is noise.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 32
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 60,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "sum"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (n8n_node_type) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_calls_total{service=~\"$service\", span_name=\"node.execute\", n8n_node_type!=\"\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{n8n_node_type}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Node errors per second by type",
      "description": "Span status, not HTTP status. A node that fails fast will not show up in the latency panels at all.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 32
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 60
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "sum"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (n8n_node_type) (rate(traces_spanmetrics_calls_total{service=~\"$service\", span_name=\"node.execute\", status_code=\"STATUS_CODE_ERROR\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{n8n_node_type}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Slow executions — click a row for the span waterfall",
      "description": "Queries Tempo directly rather than the derived metrics. This is where the per-node breakdown lives: the row opens the trace, the trace shows which node held the execution and for how long.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "${tracesource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "query": "{name=\"workflow.execute\" && duration > $min_duration}",
          "limit": 50
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "sortBy": [
          {
            "displayName": "Duration",
            "desc": true
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
